Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests Utilities list;
register(JitterT);
define
    jtAcc=0;
    jtPre=0;
    jtBadN=0;
    jtRead=0;
    jtAdd code={
        jtAcc += argument;
        };
    jtPreA code={
        jtPre += 1;
        };
    jtName; jtPending; jtRows=0; jtTrue=0; jtMark; jtSlot; jtZ;
    jtMintRow code={
        jtMark := new(argument);
        *jtMark = 0;
        jtPending +% *jtMark;
        jtSlot := jtPending[argument];
        jtRows = jtRows + 1;
        };
    jtResult code={
        jtName := argument.taG;
        jtMintRow(*jtName);
        if *jtRead == argument; *jtSlot = 1;
        if *jtSlot == 1;        jtTrue = jtTrue + 1;
        };
    jtGood code={
        jtRead := jtZ;
        jtResult(good=1);
        };
    jtBad code={
        jtZ = 0;
        ++jtZ;
        jtRead := jtZ;
        jtResult(zeroBump=1);
        jtBadN += 1;
        };
    ;
testing(jtPreA);
cerr "JT-0 compiled and fired by testing() before jitter: jtPre = [" jtPre "]":;
jitter;
jtAdd(2);
jtAdd(3);
jtAdd(4);
cerr "JT-1 three calls after jitter: jtAcc = [" jtAcc "]":;
jtGood();
jtBad();
jtBad();
cerr "JT-3 a body the JIT refuses, called twice: jtBadN = [" jtBadN "]":;
jtPreA();
jtPreA();
cerr "JT-4 compiled by testing() before jitter, two more calls: jtPre = [" jtPre "]":;
cerr "JITTER SENTINEL":;
stop();

jitterT -- SEQ 386 R3 (Tony, 2026-10-19): THE jitter; COMMAND, first cut. After `jitter;` every action is compiled at
its first call and every later call goes straight to the cache. Born red on trunk: `jitter;` is not a command there and
a bare unknown name does nothing, so the values agree and only the witness rows (the exit lines) are absent.

pop.sh reads, beside each JT row, the same file run with the `jitter;` line removed (the interpreted twin), and a twin
with parser(Start) after the last search line (the new road). The witness lines are printed by the jitter at exit
(stderr, one per action it met): `=== jitter: <action> built <n> called <m> ===`, or `NOT JITTABLE` for a refused
compile, which also announces once, by name, at the refusal.
  JT-1  jtAdd, three calls: built 1, called 3, jtAcc = 9 = the twin.
  JT-3  jtBad: its compile is refused (-5, the verifier: "Instruction does not dominate all uses"). jtGood inlines
        jtResult first; jtBad is the SECOND action to inline it, and that is what the verifier rejects -- the same
        action compiles alone (testPrecedence's tpAssignBare / tpAssignArg pair, cut down). One announcement,
        interpreted both times, jtBadN = 2. (jtResult, then called interpreted, is refused the same way.)
  JT-4  jtPreA was compiled by testing() before jitter: built 0 (reused from the cache), called 2, jtPre = 3.
